            <ArticleTitle>[Oral combination therapy of zoster neuralgia. Pain reduction by 1-adamantanamine sulfate and carbamazepine per os].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In four patients hospitalized with severe neuralgic complaints in conjunction with a Zoster infection, the pain-relieving effect of oral 1-adamantanamine sulfate used in combination with carbamazepine was studied. From the results obtained, the oral administration of 1-adamantanamine sulfate also appears to have a reliable analgesic effect, so that ambulatory treatment is readily possible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
